# Render's filesystem is ephemeral: logs/, market_state.json, baseline.json and
# any other generated local state reset on every redeploy. That's fine for a
# hackathon demo (the trading agent just re-seeds its state), but any persistent
# data you care about would need an external store (e.g. a database or object
# storage) instead. See the README for how the app recreates these at runtime.

